<!--
  Canonical price_extra backfill on product.template.attribute.value for
  the OCA-configured anchor values that customer configuration in
  /kitchen-planner and the sales-rep Order Builder rely on to re-price.

  noupdate="1" so runtime edits by the product owner in the backend UI
  survive `-u southbrook_estimating`. The seed applies on -i or a fresh
  install; subsequent upgrades leave PTAV.price_extra untouched. Same
  reactivity contract as data/room_templates.xml (Phase 6.2) and
  data/prodboard_taxonomy_seed.xml — audit §4.A pattern.

  Anchor decisions (2026-07-01, per docs/track_c_price_extra_pending_
  2026-07-01.md — landed with confident defaults, not full Price Master
  extraction):

    box_maple        — list_price × 0.10 per CLAUDE.md §5 Rule 2 (canonical)
    series_signature — 0.00 (base tier — other series price DOWN from Signature)
    door_five_piece  — $35 uniform (widely-quoted 5-piece woodgrain upgrade)
    accessory_soft_close — $15 uniform (widely-quoted Blum soft-close per-cabinet)
    drawer_metal_blum    — $65 on drawer-carrying templates (Blum Legrabox)

  Anchors DELIBERATELY OMITTED:
    finish_premium_colors — attr_finish is a NF19 placeholder set; the
      exact "premium colors" mapping needs product-owner input (see
      docs/track_c_price_extra_pending_2026-07-01.md Q1). Landing zeros
      here would create maintenance debt without customer value.

  Blast radius = customer-visible pricing. Rollback = `git revert` this
  commit + `-u southbrook_estimating`.

  Supersedes southbrook_configurator_ux/data/tactical_price_extras.xml
  (demo-grade). Delete that file + its tactical_price_seed.py once this
  seed's numbers are confirmed with the product owner and any refinements
  land — the tactical file's docstring explicitly authorises this transition.
-->
